00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:29.340
A catalyst-event strategy focuses on discrete news items that alter a company's near-term

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:35.100
cash flow outlook. Today's Raytheon Award illustrates the approach because the $20.7

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:41.860
billion US Air Force deal supplies multi-year revenue visibility that can stabilize earnings estimates.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.000
Implementation starts with screening for contract announcements on platforms like Bloomberg

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.060
or company filings. The next step checks whether the award size exceeds 10% of trailing

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.100
12-month revenue. The setup works best when the contract is with a high-credit-quality

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:03.780
customer and carries low cancellation risk. Historical examples show defense contractors

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:10.060
often re-rate higher after similar awards because analysts raise forward estimates. Risk

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.640
arises if the market has already priced the news or if sector rotation pulls capital

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.100
elsewhere.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:21.220
Pair the screen with a same-day volume check above the 20-day average before entry. This

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:26.000
This trade demonstrates how to quantify a growth milestone into a position sizing decision

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.080
while respecting volume and moving average filters.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.920
Disclaimer, this is a simulated trade for educational purposes only.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.800
No real money is involved.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.940
This is not financial advice.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:43.960
Today's pick is iag.to on the TSX in the financial sector.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:50.420
The strategy is a catalyst play on segregated fund assets crossing a $50 billion milestone

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:55.720
that signals sustained inflows. The hold period is five sessions from entry.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:00.820
In validation comes if a weekly close moves below the 50-day moving average.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.700
The catalyst is the company announcement that it surpassed $50 billion in

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.720
segregated fund assets under management in September 2026.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.160
The technical setup shows the stock above its 50-day moving average

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.980
with volume running near the 20-day average on the announcement day.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.160
The maximum acceptable loss is set at 8% from entry.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:27.200
The target is plus 3% to plus 7% over the five-session window.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:33.180
Confidence is medium because the milestone provides a clear fundamental catalyst, but sector

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.560
rotation in financials remains a variable.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:44.300
Yesterday's simulated hold was GOOGL, entered at $357.65 on the Tuesday open.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:55.920
